Note (transparency, no red-as-green): the instrumented androidTest source set is NOT part of this gate
(assembleRelease + testReleaseUnitTest do not compile androidTest). TeslaReauthBannerUiTest.kt is authored to the
known-good convention - it calls .assertDoesNotExist() as a SemanticsNodeInteraction member (no import) and
imports only top-level helpers (onNodeWithTag / onNodeWithText / onNodeWithContentDescription / assertIsDisplayed
/ assertHasClickAction / performClick), the SAME imports 19 sibling androidTest files use. It mirrors the
known-good OfflineBannerUiTest exactly.

Binding note (web parity): web TeslaReauthBanner.tsx has no data hook - it subscribes to two app-GLOBAL document
CustomEvents (teslasync:tesla-auth-expired / -recovered) and replays the teslaAuthRecovery.ts mutation queue, with
useNavigate('/tesla-account') + a local dismiss. Neither the event target nor the queue was ported to the shared
core, and the native Authentik AuthController is the SessionExpiredModal analogue (a distinct hard blocker). So
this surface owns the faithful native analogue of that global bus + queue, TeslaReauthBus (app-scoped hot event
SharedFlow + best-effort mutation replay queue, process-global instance), which external producers (a future
Tesla-401 interceptor / the tesla-account reconnect screen) dispatch onto - exactly as web resilientFetch /
TeslaAccountSection dispatch onto document. i18n binds the P1/S10 catalog (translation_tesla_reauth_title/_body/
_cta + translation_common_dismiss, exact web copy); navigation binds via onReconnect (web useNavigate, host-wired
to Destinations id teslaAccount, the same pattern TeslaAuthCard.onManage uses; no LocalNavController exists). The
web's generic loading/empty/error/stale template states do not apply to a binary event banner and fold onto the
two honest web branches reproduced here: Dormant (web 'if (!visible) return null') and Expired (the visible
warning banner). The banner is an assertive live region (web role="alert" / aria-live="assertive"); the one-shot
view.opened diagnostic (P1/S11) carries only the surface slug.

